# Working with AI to build {{ title }}

For the owner **and** the AI agent. Owner's experience: **{{ experience }}**. AI builder: **{{ agent }}**.

## Why AI-built projects fall apart (and what protects this one)

| What goes wrong | What it looks like | What's set up to prevent it |
|---|---|---|
| Giant requests | "Build the whole app" → thousands of lines nobody understands | Build plan split into small milestones; `/plan` for features |
| No tests | Every fix breaks something else | `test-writer` agent; quality gate runs tests before "done"; CI on every PR |
| Fix loops | Same file patched 10 times, bugs multiply | Loop detector hook; `/fix` protocol; `debugger` agent; revert to last green |
| Forgetting context | New session, agent redoes or undoes old work | PROGRESS.md loaded at every session start |
| Scope creep | Features and libraries nobody asked for | Stack fixed in the skill; `architect` agent pushes back; ask-first rule |
| Over-engineering | Kubernetes & microservices for 20 users | Engineering playbook marks what's NOT NEEDED for your scale |
| Leaked secrets | API key pushed to GitHub, then abused | File guard hook, git pre-commit scan, CI secret scan |
| Destroyed work | `rm -rf`, force-push, database wipe | Bash guard hook blocks destructive commands |
| "It's done!" (it isn't) | Claims success without running anything | Stop-hook quality gate; definition of done; PR checks |
| Direct edits to live app | Broken production | Branches + PRs + CI + previews; pre-push hook blocks pushing to main |

## The golden loop (every piece of work)

1. **Plan** — say what you want in normal words; the agent turns it into small steps (`/plan`).
2. **Build one step** — on a branch.
3. **Test** — automated tests + you try it (preview link or locally).
4. **Review** — `code-reviewer` agent; `security-auditor` for logins, data, payments, AI.
5. **Commit & PR** — CI must be green.
6. **Merge & check** — production deploys automatically; 1-minute check that it works.
7. **Update PROGRESS.md** — so the next session knows where we are.

## What was set up for you (plain words)
{% if agent_is_claude %}
| Piece | What it does |
|---|---|
| **Session-start hook** | Reminds the AI of the plan, progress and branch every time you open a session. |
| **Bash guard hook** | Blocks dangerous commands (deleting everything, force-push, pushing to main, wiping databases, printing secrets). |
| **File guard hook** | Blocks writing secrets into code, editing `.env`, hand-editing lockfiles, or weakening the safety net. |
| **Post-edit hook** | Auto-formats every file the AI changes; warns it when it's stuck in a fix loop. |
| **Quality gate (stop hook)** | Before the AI says "done", runs lint/typecheck/tests; sends it back once to fix failures. |
| **Helper agents** | `architect` (plans), `test-writer`, `code-reviewer`, `debugger`, `security-auditor`. |
| **Commands** | `/plan`, `/fix`, `/ship`, `/explain`, `/status`. |
